2. DEVELOPMENT CONSTRAINTS

Use the following priorities.

1. The game must run in a modern Android browser.
2. Use React and TypeScript for the application interface.
3. Prefer Three.js for real-time 3D rendering.
4. Use supported npm packages where genuinely useful.
5. Keep the first version playable without requiring a login, external account, or paid game asset.
6. Create original procedural 3D models wherever possible.
7. Keep the first version small enough to run on a mid-range Android phone.
8. Avoid dependencies on desktop-only editors or tools.
9. Do not require manual installation of external assets merely to start a match.
10. Do not expose API keys or private credentials in browser code.

Inspect the existing project before changing its architecture.

If a suitable project already exists, extend it rather than unnecessarily rebuilding everything.

If a requested library is incompatible with the environment, choose a reliable alternative.

Use the available build, preview, and debugging capabilities to identify and correct errors.

Do not falsely claim that a feature works unless you have implemented and tested it.

